WEBVTT

00:00:27.030 --> 00:00:28.240
<i>A long time ago,</i>

00:00:28.950 --> 00:00:31.240
<i>I heard a strange sound in the mountains.</i>

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:42.790
The ring of a bell?

00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:52.590
Now it's ringing all over the mountain.

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:08.440
<i>For a while, the sound of countless bells ringing</i>

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:12.200
<i>echoed across the mountains.</i>

00:01:26.540 --> 00:01:31.340
<i>It felt as though the entire mountain was celebrating something.</i>

00:01:34.390 --> 00:01:41.310
Belldrops

00:01:46.020 --> 00:01:48.070
<i>Ten months later,</i>

00:01:48.070 --> 00:01:50.030
<i>my little sister was born.</i>

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:55.820
Was the baby born safely?

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:20.010
They seem strange and alien.

00:02:20.970 --> 00:02:23.430
Primitive and peculiar,

00:02:23.430 --> 00:02:29.610
they are unlike any flora or fauna known to us.

00:02:30.190 --> 00:02:33.110
From time immemorial,

00:02:33.820 --> 00:02:37.110
men have feared these misshapen entities,

00:02:37.910 --> 00:02:43.450
which came to be known as "mushi."

00:02:40.120 --> 00:02:48.960
Mushi

00:03:08.440 --> 00:03:11.690
We broke

00:03:10.810 --> 00:03:13.750
Everything that was right

00:03:12.870 --> 00:03:16.570
We both enjoyed a good fight

00:03:16.270 --> 00:03:19.580
And we solved

00:03:18.700 --> 00:03:21.510
All the holes we had to breathe

00:03:20.630 --> 00:03:24.530
To make the other one leave

00:03:24.110 --> 00:03:27.400
And I loved

00:03:26.520 --> 00:03:30.530
The way you looked at me

00:03:31.750 --> 00:03:35.190
And I miss

00:03:34.310 --> 00:03:38.140
The way you made me feel

00:03:37.260 --> 00:03:40.570
When we were alone

00:03:45.690 --> 00:03:52.680
And I'll shiver like I used to

00:03:53.580 --> 00:04:00.060
And I'll leave him just for you

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:08.300
And I'll shiver like I used to

00:04:05.620 --> 00:04:20.720
Mushi-Shi

00:04:08.680 --> 00:04:15.950
Just for you

00:04:16.510 --> 00:04:23.420
Like I used to

00:04:52.420 --> 00:04:54.840
<i>I'm being watched.</i>

00:05:03.010 --> 00:05:04.470
<i>This mountain's thriving.</i>

00:05:05.260 --> 00:05:07.220
<i>Does a River of Light pass through it?</i>

00:05:10.020 --> 00:05:13.020
<i>If so, there should be a lord around here.</i>

00:05:35.500 --> 00:05:36.670
<i>It can't be.</i>

00:05:53.350 --> 00:05:54.190
<i>There.</i>

00:05:55.400 --> 00:05:56.810
<i>A lord's path.</i>

00:07:14.310 --> 00:07:15.770
Don't push yourself.

00:07:17.190 --> 00:07:19.020
You're rather malnourished.

00:07:22.320 --> 00:07:24.400
I'm Ginko, a mushi-shi.

00:07:24.820 --> 00:07:27.780
I figured I'd greet you
while passing through this mountain.

00:07:29.490 --> 00:07:31.780
That's a nutritious potion.

00:07:33.240 --> 00:07:36.080
It should work on the mushi too.

00:07:43.000 --> 00:07:47.170
Why are you acting as the lord here?

00:07:48.630 --> 00:07:51.350
People being chosen as lords

00:07:51.350 --> 00:07:53.430
is something I've only seen in old archives.

00:07:54.970 --> 00:07:57.940
And none of them survived for long.

00:07:58.980 --> 00:08:02.190
You seem to be rather weakened yourself.

00:08:03.190 --> 00:08:04.190
Begone.

00:08:17.200 --> 00:08:20.750
<i>Looks like I shouldn't dig too deep.</i>

00:08:40.270 --> 00:08:41.650
Are you a traveler?

00:08:41.650 --> 00:08:42.350
Yeah.

00:08:43.860 --> 00:08:45.230
Um...

00:08:45.230 --> 00:08:47.610
Did you see a girl in the mountains?

00:08:48.190 --> 00:08:50.320
Around fourteen years of age.

00:08:50.320 --> 00:08:51.740
A girl?

00:08:51.740 --> 00:08:53.620
Did she get lost?

00:08:55.200 --> 00:08:56.410
I don't know.

00:08:56.410 --> 00:08:59.540
She suddenly disappeared one day.

00:09:02.120 --> 00:09:05.040
What was she like?

00:09:08.170 --> 00:09:11.510
She's probably just as I remember her.

00:09:15.640 --> 00:09:20.680
<i>From the moment my sister was born,
she had weeds growing out of her head.</i>

00:09:23.690 --> 00:09:27.270
<i>No matter how many we pulled out,
they always grew back.</i>

00:09:29.940 --> 00:09:32.030
<i>Once she became able to walk,</i>

00:09:32.030 --> 00:09:35.410
<i>she'd often sneak out of home alone.</i>

00:09:36.580 --> 00:09:37.900
Hey, Kaya!

00:09:40.160 --> 00:09:41.910
You went out by yourself again, didn't you?

00:09:42.660 --> 00:09:45.170
Just where did you think you were going?

00:09:45.920 --> 00:09:47.040
Kaya!

00:09:47.040 --> 00:09:49.090
How many times do I have to repeat myself?

00:09:49.090 --> 00:09:50.920
You'll get lost again, you hear me?

00:09:51.760 --> 00:09:52.930
Yoshirou,

00:09:52.930 --> 00:09:55.430
look out for Kaya.

00:09:56.010 --> 00:09:57.470
Could you do that for me?

00:10:03.850 --> 00:10:05.230
Listen, Kaya.

00:10:05.230 --> 00:10:07.560
Don't go running off by yourself.

00:10:09.730 --> 00:10:11.570
There aren't many to be found.

00:10:14.280 --> 00:10:15.780
Brother.

00:10:19.990 --> 00:10:21.500
Whoa!

00:10:24.500 --> 00:10:26.080
Good job finding this place.

00:10:26.920 --> 00:10:28.590
I'm proud of you.

00:10:35.630 --> 00:10:36.930
Huh?

00:10:36.930 --> 00:10:39.100
Did we go the wrong way?

00:10:44.430 --> 00:10:45.350
Kaya?

00:10:48.900 --> 00:10:50.650
Do you know the way home?

00:10:54.440 --> 00:10:59.410
<i>For some reason, my sister knew this mountain like the back of her own hand.</i>

00:11:02.490 --> 00:11:05.910
<i>But she'd say the strangest things at times.</i>

00:11:09.130 --> 00:11:10.750
What's wrong, Kaya?

00:11:14.340 --> 00:11:16.300
They're beckoning me.

00:11:20.470 --> 00:11:23.720
They're telling me to come back.

00:11:29.520 --> 00:11:30.810
<i>Not only that,</i>

00:11:32.570 --> 00:11:36.320
<i>she also had frequent spells
where it felt like her mind was elsewhere. </i>

00:11:39.160 --> 00:11:40.450
Kaya!

00:11:40.450 --> 00:11:42.160
Pull yourself together, Kaya!

00:11:44.620 --> 00:11:47.160
<i>She would eventually go back to normal,</i>

00:11:47.160 --> 00:11:49.540
<i>but she seemed awfully weakened each time.</i>

00:11:52.340 --> 00:11:53.420
Here.

00:11:53.420 --> 00:11:55.170
I pounded some rice cakes for you.

00:11:55.880 --> 00:11:58.340
Eat these, and get well soon.

00:12:05.560 --> 00:12:07.270
It's getting windy.

00:12:10.560 --> 00:12:12.480
We should hurry home.

00:12:23.080 --> 00:12:24.200
Are you all right?

00:12:29.000 --> 00:12:30.210
Kaya?

00:12:31.290 --> 00:12:32.710
Where are you, Kaya?

00:12:33.840 --> 00:12:35.090
Kaya!

00:12:36.550 --> 00:12:38.300
<i>That was the last I saw of her.</i>

00:12:41.260 --> 00:12:44.180
<i>We searched all over the mountain,
but we couldn't find her.</i>

00:12:45.430 --> 00:12:47.220
<i>However, after that,</i>

00:12:47.220 --> 00:12:51.730
<i>we started to find tiny footsteps
on the mountain every now and then.</i>

00:12:55.070 --> 00:13:01.240
So I'm still looking for her every chance I get.

00:13:03.240 --> 00:13:09.540
I can't shake the feeling
that she's lost up here, all by herself.

00:13:13.380 --> 00:13:17.000
I don't think she's ever coming back.

00:13:18.630 --> 00:13:20.260
How can you say that?

00:13:23.430 --> 00:13:29.270
We mushi-shi call thriving lands like these "Rivers of Light."

00:13:30.810 --> 00:13:34.770
Each one requires a lord to oversee it.

00:13:36.270 --> 00:13:41.570
When a person is chosen to be that lord,
they're born with weeds growing on their bodies.

00:13:44.320 --> 00:13:47.160
A lord? What's a lord?

00:13:50.870 --> 00:13:54.830
A being that maintains
the ecological balance of a mountain.

00:13:55.630 --> 00:14:00.050
They're linked to the entire mountain at all times
and constantly act to regulate it.

00:14:01.210 --> 00:14:04.720
They're the mountain's foundation, so to speak.

00:14:05.390 --> 00:14:07.050
They don't exist as individuals.

00:14:08.060 --> 00:14:09.430
I hate to say this,

00:14:09.430 --> 00:14:11.310
but looking for her is a waste of time.

00:14:12.600 --> 00:14:16.310
Your sister can no longer return to the village.

00:14:17.610 --> 00:14:21.940
Surely you yourself were aware
your sister was no ordinary child.

00:14:22.570 --> 00:14:25.860
Kaya's just a girl.

00:14:27.700 --> 00:14:31.450
Approach the lord too lightly,
and the entire mountain will fall apart.

00:14:31.910 --> 00:14:34.710
Your lives will be ruined if that happens.

00:14:52.600 --> 00:14:54.680
<i>She hasn't come back here, huh?</i>

00:14:55.890 --> 00:14:57.650
<i>Where could she have gone in that state?</i>

00:15:03.190 --> 00:15:04.900
Kaya!

00:15:13.910 --> 00:15:17.000
<i>Your sister was no ordinary child.</i>

00:15:24.760 --> 00:15:28.140
You're my sister. Nothing more.

00:15:49.360 --> 00:15:50.370
Hey.

00:15:50.370 --> 00:15:51.910
Did the potion help?

00:15:56.250 --> 00:15:57.960
You want more?

00:15:58.670 --> 00:16:00.960
Unfortunately, that was all I had on me.

00:16:00.960 --> 00:16:03.460
I'm looking for the herbs I need to make more.

00:16:28.570 --> 00:16:33.580
Did you know that your brother
from the village is still looking for you?

00:16:35.620 --> 00:16:40.580
If you do run into each other, make sure
not to concern yourself with him anymore.

00:16:47.420 --> 00:16:48.840
I see.

00:16:50.340 --> 00:16:51.890
You've already forgotten, huh?

00:16:52.470 --> 00:16:54.100
Your heart will,

00:16:57.470 --> 00:16:59.230
over time,

00:16:59.230 --> 00:17:03.730
gradually be crushed by the weight of the mountain

00:17:08.940 --> 00:17:13.280
and lose its humanity.

00:17:29.550 --> 00:17:30.630
Oh no!

00:17:30.630 --> 00:17:31.630
Wolves?

00:17:41.850 --> 00:17:42.520
Damn it!

00:17:46.820 --> 00:17:48.150
<i>Did I miss?</i>

00:17:52.950 --> 00:17:54.450
<i>They're leaving.</i>

00:18:08.750 --> 00:18:09.960
Kaya!

00:18:20.390 --> 00:18:21.770
<i>Where did she go?</i>

00:18:26.020 --> 00:18:28.980
<i>Don't tell me the gunshot earlier...</i>

00:18:51.130 --> 00:18:52.090
Kaya!

00:18:52.710 --> 00:18:54.840
Thank goodness you came to.

00:18:55.260 --> 00:18:57.470
Don't get up yet.

00:18:58.390 --> 00:18:59.680
Kaya?

00:18:59.680 --> 00:19:01.720
Is it really you, Kaya?

00:19:02.220 --> 00:19:03.770
I'm sorry.

00:19:04.180 --> 00:19:06.520
The bullet didn't hit you, thankfully.

00:19:06.520 --> 00:19:08.020
But it must have scared you.

00:19:09.110 --> 00:19:12.070
Here. Your favorite rice cakes.

00:19:12.070 --> 00:19:13.740
Eat these, and get better.

00:19:23.240 --> 00:19:25.580
You were alone in the mountain for so long.

00:19:26.460 --> 00:19:29.170
You must have been lonely and scared.

00:19:31.040 --> 00:19:34.460
But you'll never have to feel that way again.

00:19:37.430 --> 00:19:38.720
Come, Kaya.

00:19:38.720 --> 00:19:40.260
Try this on.

00:19:43.930 --> 00:19:45.270
It's a perfect fit!

00:19:46.640 --> 00:19:50.770
I made it for you to wear whenever you returned.

00:19:51.560 --> 00:19:54.530
Look, Kaya. You have a little brother.

00:19:54.530 --> 00:19:56.990
Your sister's back with us.

00:20:13.750 --> 00:20:16.510
<i>I've got a bad feeling about this fog.</i>

00:20:21.550 --> 00:20:23.050
<i>What's with these weeds?</i>

00:20:23.600 --> 00:20:25.270
Did you hear?

00:20:27.140 --> 00:20:30.060
Apparently Yoshirou's sister is back.

00:20:30.060 --> 00:20:31.310
Really?

00:20:31.860 --> 00:20:33.400
She's still alive?

00:20:44.990 --> 00:20:46.490
Look.

00:20:46.490 --> 00:20:48.660
She's clearly human.

00:20:51.370 --> 00:20:53.590
You're wrong about her.

00:20:55.500 --> 00:20:58.010
Just leave her alone.

00:21:00.880 --> 00:21:02.970
Haven't they returned yet?

00:21:02.970 --> 00:21:06.510
No. They said they'd be right back, too.

00:21:06.510 --> 00:21:08.600
It's not like them to get lost.

00:21:09.100 --> 00:21:10.690
Something must have happened.

00:21:32.420 --> 00:21:35.000
The weeds have already grown so much.

00:21:36.590 --> 00:21:39.460
The mountain's falling into chaos.

00:21:44.050 --> 00:21:45.600
How strange.

00:21:45.600 --> 00:21:47.010
We're back at the cliff again.

00:21:47.010 --> 00:21:48.770
Hey!

00:21:48.770 --> 00:21:50.270
Anybody there?!

00:21:50.270 --> 00:21:51.980
Hey!

00:21:51.980 --> 00:21:53.390
Anybody there?!

00:21:53.390 --> 00:21:55.150
Why is the echo coming from <i>behind</i> us?

00:21:58.650 --> 00:21:59.900
Monkeys?

00:22:01.780 --> 00:22:02.900
Look.

00:22:03.990 --> 00:22:06.900
The river's glowing.

00:22:37.610 --> 00:22:39.180
This is bad.

00:22:40.920 --> 00:22:42.780
The mountain's going to die.

00:23:06.050 --> 00:23:07.340
Kaya?

00:23:40.920 --> 00:23:44.010
<i>The fog's clearing.</i>

00:23:56.890 --> 00:23:57.890
So you're back.

00:24:03.730 --> 00:24:06.360
It came to get me.

00:24:08.490 --> 00:24:09.410
"It"?

00:24:10.870 --> 00:24:12.410
The circle of light.

00:24:14.370 --> 00:24:17.250
Messenger of the mountain's will.

00:24:18.750 --> 00:24:23.540
All a lord does is obey.

00:24:27.510 --> 00:24:31.430
I must return the mountain to normal.

00:24:32.100 --> 00:24:33.550
Can you handle it?

00:24:35.430 --> 00:24:39.140
I'll just do what I've been doing all this while.

00:24:43.020 --> 00:24:46.860
This may not be any consolation at all,

00:24:47.610 --> 00:24:49.700
but I'm glad to have met you.

00:24:51.700 --> 00:24:53.530
Plants, mushi,

00:24:53.530 --> 00:24:55.450
animals, and people...

00:24:55.450 --> 00:24:57.950
We all live our lives bound by nature's laws.

00:24:59.160 --> 00:25:01.080
That's how it's always been.

00:25:03.080 --> 00:25:05.090
And I'm sure that's how it'll always be.

00:25:06.460 --> 00:25:09.630
Lords are embodiments of that arrangement,

00:25:12.180 --> 00:25:15.470
and seeing one in the shape of a human

00:25:16.810 --> 00:25:20.480
brought me great joy.

00:25:23.100 --> 00:25:25.060
Take care.

00:25:25.940 --> 00:25:28.070
I'll be back soon.

00:25:35.120 --> 00:25:36.280
Ginko?

00:25:38.950 --> 00:25:41.210
She said she'd return to the mountain.

00:25:43.080 --> 00:25:47.130
Getting too attached to the village
will only make her suffer.

00:25:48.760 --> 00:25:50.470
You shouldn't see her anymore.

00:25:51.300 --> 00:25:53.130
That's what's best for all of you.

00:25:59.220 --> 00:26:04.100
Is that all I can do for Kaya?

00:26:06.980 --> 00:26:08.820
Why does it have to be her?

00:26:10.740 --> 00:26:13.150
Why was she chosen?

00:26:17.330 --> 00:26:21.790
I can't forget her.

00:26:22.910 --> 00:26:24.670
You don't have to.

00:26:25.420 --> 00:26:27.130
Keep her in your thoughts.

00:26:28.460 --> 00:26:30.800
The lord and mountain alike

00:26:30.800 --> 00:26:32.970
will always be watching over you.

00:26:35.680 --> 00:26:37.510
Within every plant,

00:26:38.140 --> 00:26:40.180
mushi, and animal

00:26:41.270 --> 00:26:43.180
are Kaya's eyes and ears.

00:26:45.690 --> 00:26:49.150
Don't forget that, ever.

00:27:08.580 --> 00:27:10.420
I'll go get some firewood.

00:27:29.360 --> 00:27:31.400
Are you well, Kaya?

00:28:23.530 --> 00:28:24.830
After you left,

00:28:24.830 --> 00:28:27.750
strange things started happening on the mountain again.

00:28:29.870 --> 00:28:32.670
The animals are on edge, and the plants are drying out.

00:28:34.250 --> 00:28:37.510
My brother's been in bad shape lately, too.

00:28:39.680 --> 00:28:42.300
I haven't seen Kaya at all.

00:28:44.100 --> 00:28:46.720
Did something happen to her?

00:28:50.520 --> 00:28:52.980
Give your brother this medicine.

00:28:56.530 --> 00:28:59.240
I'll go see how she's doing.

00:29:10.920 --> 00:29:12.380
Kaya!

00:29:13.000 --> 00:29:14.500
What's wrong?

00:29:14.500 --> 00:29:16.000
Are you all right?

00:29:26.470 --> 00:29:27.520
Kaya?

00:29:48.240 --> 00:29:51.040
What in the world happened?

00:29:53.500 --> 00:29:56.920
I can't hear the mountain's voice anymore.

00:29:58.800 --> 00:30:02.680
I can't be one with it.

00:30:04.550 --> 00:30:10.730
I can't tell how to return the mountain to normal.

00:30:13.310 --> 00:30:19.070
So I'm sure my successor will be chosen soon.

00:30:19.400 --> 00:30:21.070
Your successor?

00:30:21.070 --> 00:30:23.030
What happens to you?

00:30:25.610 --> 00:30:29.200
The old lord will be consumed by the mountain

00:30:30.660 --> 00:30:33.710
in order to give the next one strength.

00:30:40.460 --> 00:30:45.340
Is that the mountain's law?

00:30:46.260 --> 00:30:48.970
Talk about cruel.

00:30:50.100 --> 00:30:54.020
All you did was yearn for your family—

00:30:56.270 --> 00:30:58.440
something all humans do.

00:31:00.230 --> 00:31:02.780
If you couldn't be allowed even that,

00:31:02.780 --> 00:31:05.360
then you should never have been chosen as the lord.

00:31:06.910 --> 00:31:13.040
Those weeds are a sign that a new lord has been chosen.

00:31:14.250 --> 00:31:17.500
They enter them at birth

00:31:17.500 --> 00:31:19.540
and ring out in beautiful harmony.

00:31:21.420 --> 00:31:23.170
They haven't borne fruit yet.

00:31:24.920 --> 00:31:31.140
If you can return the lord's power to the mountain before they do, your life should be spared.

00:31:32.180 --> 00:31:35.480
You can just live a human life afterward.

00:31:38.190 --> 00:31:39.860
A human life...

00:31:43.150 --> 00:31:45.150
I don't know if it will work,

00:31:45.950 --> 00:31:50.700
but let me have a quiet word with the law.

00:32:03.880 --> 00:32:05.170
All done.

00:32:06.630 --> 00:32:08.680
This is a strong mushi purge.

00:32:11.510 --> 00:32:14.970
Drink this, and the weeds linking you to the mountain should grow out.

00:32:16.730 --> 00:32:18.600
It'll be a bit painful.

00:33:07.650 --> 00:33:09.820
Heed me, law.

00:33:10.650 --> 00:33:12.240
I offer you the lord's power.

00:33:13.280 --> 00:33:14.740
Please accept it,

00:33:16.410 --> 00:33:20.210
and spare your human lord.

00:34:08.880 --> 00:34:11.170
This is not the lord.

00:34:14.010 --> 00:34:16.800
Why is an ordinary human here?

00:34:22.230 --> 00:34:25.230
He returned the lord's power.

00:34:25.940 --> 00:34:28.440
Did the creepers mistake him for a lord?

00:34:29.360 --> 00:34:33.030
This is a mushi banquet—

00:34:34.410 --> 00:34:35.990
a circle of light.

00:34:38.870 --> 00:34:42.200
Nothing good comes of getting involved with humans.

00:34:44.000 --> 00:34:47.040
They possess strange wisdom.

00:34:51.510 --> 00:34:55.050
We should never have made one a lord.

00:34:56.260 --> 00:34:59.310
Even the law can make mistakes.

00:35:00.390 --> 00:35:01.680
That's right.

00:35:01.680 --> 00:35:03.680
You should never have made her a lord.

00:35:04.810 --> 00:35:07.060
So you can have the lord's power back.

00:35:07.060 --> 00:35:09.360
Please spare her life.

00:35:10.270 --> 00:35:15.570
You're at fault for choosing her, a human, to be a lord.

00:35:16.410 --> 00:35:19.660
Not only do humans possess wisdom,
but they also have hearts.

00:35:19.660 --> 00:35:22.650
Even if they're broken down
to form a mountain's foundation,

00:35:22.650 --> 00:35:25.210
the dimmest of lights can revive them.

00:35:26.620 --> 00:35:28.170
That's what makes them frail—

00:35:30.590 --> 00:35:34.590
incapable of fully becoming a mountain's lord.

00:35:38.180 --> 00:35:42.260
Even so, humans have functioned as lords in the past.

00:35:45.770 --> 00:35:49.730
Perhaps that is why we thought it would work once again.

00:35:52.520 --> 00:35:55.320
However, it did not.

00:35:56.400 --> 00:36:00.740
Humans will never give birth to a lord again.

00:36:06.120 --> 00:36:11.460
Consequently, they will grow
disconnected from the mountain.

00:36:13.420 --> 00:36:16.720
They will become deaf to the mountain's voice.

00:36:22.970 --> 00:36:26.020
Should such beings be allowed to exist?

00:36:26.810 --> 00:36:28.390
They won't grow disconnected.

00:36:28.390 --> 00:36:29.600
Absolutely not.

00:36:30.850 --> 00:36:34.900
Because humans, too, are just another part of the mountain.

00:36:38.780 --> 00:36:40.360
Very well.

00:36:41.120 --> 00:36:44.080
The law shall decide eventually.

00:36:47.290 --> 00:36:53.840
However, this one's actions have distorted the law.

00:37:00.300 --> 00:37:06.100
We must return it to how it is supposed to be.

00:37:12.310 --> 00:37:14.060
I came prepared for that.

00:37:20.610 --> 00:37:25.120
Then come with us.

00:37:47.600 --> 00:37:49.140
Please wait.

00:37:56.320 --> 00:37:57.480
Why are you here?!

00:37:58.980 --> 00:38:03.360
This is between the mountain and me.

00:38:06.240 --> 00:38:08.870
I won't let anyone take my place.

00:38:10.120 --> 00:38:11.750
You did nothing wrong!

00:38:12.210 --> 00:38:13.670
You don't have to go!

00:38:15.960 --> 00:38:20.840
I've always been one with this mountain.

00:38:24.380 --> 00:38:27.930
I was the plants,

00:38:27.930 --> 00:38:29.560
the mushi,

00:38:29.560 --> 00:38:31.350
the fish,

00:38:31.350 --> 00:38:33.140
and the animals.

00:38:34.650 --> 00:38:38.940
I experienced innumerable lives and deaths.

00:38:43.450 --> 00:38:44.950
And in the end,

00:38:45.490 --> 00:38:47.910
I even experienced life as a human.

00:38:48.950 --> 00:38:51.040
That doesn't mean you should die!

00:38:52.620 --> 00:38:54.500
I'm not going to.

00:38:57.630 --> 00:39:00.130
I'll just cease to be myself.

00:39:01.920 --> 00:39:05.130
I'll simply return to the arrangement

00:39:06.260 --> 00:39:14.850
that connects the mountain, life, and nature's law.

00:39:16.520 --> 00:39:17.150
Wait!

00:39:34.120 --> 00:39:36.290
<i>What is that?</i>

00:39:52.810 --> 00:39:54.520
<i>The ring of a bell?</i>

00:39:56.690 --> 00:40:00.230
<i>Was it the same as back then?</i>

00:40:29.340 --> 00:40:33.720
<i>When I was a child, this sound made my heart race.</i>

00:40:35.220 --> 00:40:38.600
<i>But now, it feels incredibly sad.</i>

00:40:43.190 --> 00:40:47.490
<i>A beautiful, sorrowful harmony</i>

00:40:48.200 --> 00:40:50.290
<i>that tears my heart to shreds.</i>

00:41:04.250 --> 00:41:05.880
<i>I need to get back.</i>

00:41:07.710 --> 00:41:10.880
<i>But what is this place, really?</i>

00:41:36.280 --> 00:41:38.910
<i>Ah. I see now.</i>

00:41:41.670 --> 00:41:43.210
<i>I know this place well.</i>

00:41:45.460 --> 00:41:48.670
<i>It lies behind our second pair of eyelids.</i>

00:42:05.440 --> 00:42:07.230
Brother!

00:42:08.110 --> 00:42:09.690
I'll come with you!

00:42:13.360 --> 00:42:15.570
Is that for Sis?

00:42:16.180 --> 00:42:17.010
Yeah.

00:42:18.080 --> 00:42:20.580
Where did she go?

00:42:23.250 --> 00:42:25.580
Somewhere we can never reach.

00:42:27.590 --> 00:42:29.250
But she's not far away.

00:42:30.210 --> 00:42:32.130
She's always right by our sides.

00:42:35.180 --> 00:42:36.260
Hey.

00:42:39.010 --> 00:42:40.600
Long time no see.

00:42:42.180 --> 00:42:45.100
Nothing out of the ordinary
has happened on the mountain lately.

00:42:48.190 --> 00:42:52.110
The new lord must be keeping it safe.

00:42:55.570 --> 00:42:56.820
See you.

00:42:56.820 --> 00:42:58.580
You're leaving already?

00:42:58.580 --> 00:43:00.120
After I take a look around.

00:43:02.560 --> 00:43:05.170
I'm sure there won't be any need,

00:43:05.170 --> 00:43:07.380
but call for me if you ever run into problems again.

00:43:13.800 --> 00:43:15.380
<i>Mountains,</i>

00:43:24.810 --> 00:43:26.560
<i>beings,</i>

00:43:37.700 --> 00:43:40.990
<i>and nature's laws are bound by an arrangement,</i>

00:44:01.260 --> 00:44:04.180
<i>and within it, we live.</i>

00:46:28.240 --> 00:46:31.330
Guess I should get going.

00:46:52.770 --> 00:46:56.480
Belldrops
